WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.640
So, let me ask you a question
about this brave new world of yours.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.920
When you've killed all the bad guys...

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.720
and when it's all perfect and just
and fair,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.040
when you have finally got it
exactly the way you want it,

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.640
what are you going to do
with the people like you?

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:20.560
The troublemakers.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.680
How are you going to protect
your glorious revolution...

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.480
from the next one?

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.320
We'll win.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:34.760
Oh, will you?
Well, maybe... maybe you will win!

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.200
But nobody wins for long.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.560
The wheel just keeps turning.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:43.360
So, come on.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.600
Break the cycle.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.160
Why are you still talking?

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:51.000
Because I want to get you to see
and I'm almost there!

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.920
Do you know what I see, Doctor?

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:56.760
A box.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:59.720
A box with everything I need.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.160
A 50% chance.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.400
For us, too.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.920
And we're off! Fingers on buzzers!
Are you feeling lucky?

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.800
Are you ready to play the game?
Who's going to be quickest?

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:12.760
-Who's going to be luckiest?
-This is not a game!

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:16.440
No, it's not a game, sweetheart,
and I mean that most sincerely.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:17.560
Why are you doing this?

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.800
Yes, I'd quite like to know that, too.
You set this up, why?

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.720
Because it's not a game, Kate.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.400
This is a scale model of war...

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:30.200
every war ever fought
right there in front of you...

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.280
Because it's always the same.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:36.560
When you fire that first shot,
no matter how right you feel,

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.000
you have no idea who's going to die!

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:43.840
You don't know whose children
are going to scream and burn!

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.040
How many hearts will be broken!

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:50.480
How many lives shattered!

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.920
How much blood will spill
until everybody does

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.560
what they were always going to have
to do from the very beginning,

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:57.840
sit down and talk!

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:05.920
Listen to me. Listen, I just...
I just want you to think.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.200
Do you know what thinking is?

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.880
It's just a fancy word
for changing your mind.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.440
I will not change my mind.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:15.960
Then you will die stupid.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.880
Alternatively,
you could step away from that box.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:25.440
You can walk right out of that door
and you could stand your revolution down.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:26.440
No!

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.000
I'm not stopping this, Doctor.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.800
I started it. I will not stop it.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.280
You think they'll let me go
after what I've done?

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.800
You're all the same, you screaming kids,
you know that?

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:39.040
"Look at me, I'm unforgiveable."

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.480
Well, here's the unforeseeable.
I forgive you...

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.360
after all you've done...

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:47.600
I forgive you.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:51.960
You don't understand.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.760
You will never understand.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.320
I don't understand?

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.600
Are you kidding? Me?
Of course I understand.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.600
You mean, you call this a war?
This funny little thing?

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.680
This is not a war!

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.720
I fought in a bigger war
than you will ever know!

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.160
I did worse things
than you could ever imagine.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.160
And when I close my eyes...

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:19.800
I hear more screams
than anyone could ever be able to count!

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:22.080
And you know
what you do with all that pain?

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.560
Shall I tell you where you put it?

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.360
You hold it tight...

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.120
till it burns your hand...

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:31.880
and you say this...

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:37.000
No one else
will ever have to live like this!

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.800
No one else will have to feel this pain!

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:42.040
Not on my watch!

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:56.720
Thank you.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:03:59.120
Thank you.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:06.960
Don't forget to subscribe to the official
Doctor Who YouTube channel.

